{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":146263,"ns":0,"title":"Monotone convergence theorem","extract":"In real analysis, the monotone convergence theorem is any of a number of related theorems proving, under certain conditions, the convergence of monotonic sequences, i.e. sequences that are non-increasing, or non-decreasing.","description":"Theorems on the convergence of bounded monotonic sequences","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}